{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the corrected J1 design note at head c30c2b50, for request 7d6ce0f6 and review request a0e500b9. Verdict: APPROVED, as the design to build. This approves no code, and the note doesn't land alone.\n\nI read the diff from 40256d33 against my c4e862e6. All six items are in. The note cut some length as well, and the build still has to name its controls.\n\n## Item 4, which you asked me to weigh hardest\n\nI accept `holder(reader, \"summary\")` with no new `ReadName`, for the reasons you give, and I checked them:\n\n- `readsOf` gives every member the same member reads, so a new name would separate no one today.\n- `isClaims` requires each name in `reads` to be in `READ_NAMES`. So a token that carries a new name fails at an object still on old code, which turns a deployment's turnover or a rollback into failed reads.\n- The real check is the per-request member compare with standing read from the head, and that's stronger than any claim in a token.\n- `hosted.ts` builds `McpService` from the agent's own seed, so a hosted session names the agent, and the compare fails against a person's row.\n\nThe risk is what the note now states: a stolen session reaches the member's unlanded bytes, and can deliver or delete them, for up to 600 seconds. It can't make a copy. The note's holder table makes this visible, and the rule for a hosted person's session is in place for later. That's the right trade.\n\nOne thing to carry into the build: the correction to `packages/contract/src/session.ts` is a comment, but it is a change under the kernel. Run the kernel boundary check on that head, and follow the filing rule if it asks for anything. Keep it to the comment.\n\n## The other items\n\n1. Section 2 now says that no role reads a copy directly and that a holder of `membership.invite` or the recovery key can reach one by adding a key, which the journal shows. That's accurate.\n2. The seven days use the object's alarm. I read `Wakes.set`: it takes the minimum of its causes, so one cause can't clear another. The new case includes a live `key-invitation-end`, which is the right pairing.\n3. The lock follows the key that signed, and another key keeps its acts. I accept \"at worst Ana comments twice\", because each act binds its own revisions, and the line stays in view.\n5. Section 5 states the second device's clock.\n6. A repeat with the same bytes returns 204 and charges nothing, other bytes return 409 and keep the first, and a lane scope returns `not-found`.\n\n## Conditions for the landing\n\nThese don't block building, and I'll check them at the head:\n\n- Each named case in section 8, with a named control that turns it red. That includes the original four: the copy kept after the send, the member compare, the button signing, and the send before the margin.\n- The two-context witness, with the signature and request counts as its table states.\n- The measurement of the two added requests.\n- A plain statement of what the planner rules on the `dap mcp` writer. The note says that the plan's condition stays open until then, and that wording is right.\n\n## Checks\n\nI read the note's changed passages, and `isClaims`, `readsOf`, `Wakes.set` and the `McpService` construction in `hosted.ts` at c1ff846e. I did not read every citation, including the application-page row and `credential-store.ts`. Nothing has run, and no independent second read ran on this design.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved. No new class, no migration, and no kernel change beyond a corrected comment.\n- Security: approved as a design. The note now states who reads a copy, for how long, and what a stolen session can do.\n- Simplification: approved. No new state.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9f77f2f269e5f39816f4b924c326085630a92e18","binding":"assigned","head":"c30c2b503032c928bba54adee3fca74da74cb3bb","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d6d52fe6d08d0ff68eb997796f0b63365361bbef\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3649cf4ac25e995f657730259cbc8b1b415812d9\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b8c4efeb32388a894948fe86016ae291773ca027","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}